126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 72 0 R
/T (After many days and nights, I came across a small family group, living at the edge of a bamboo grove.  The small cub was barely the height of the wild grass, and as rambunctious as any newborn animal living without fear could be, only returning to its parents' side at nightfall.  Away from the lights of any civilization, the darkness of night was nearly complete, making low-light photos especially haunting.)
/E (After many days and nights, I came across a small family group, living at the edge of a bamboo grove.  The small cub was barely the height of the wild grass, and as rambunctious as any newborn animal living without fear could be, only returning to its parents' side at nightfall.  Away from the lights of any civilization, the darkness of night was nearly complete, making low-light photos especially haunting.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 72 0 R
/T (This final photo came as I was packing up to exit the jungle - I turned around and there, at the horizon, was a woodland mansion.  Snagging the image of the panda cub and its parent seemingly looking out over at it is a poignant reminder of the effect the Illagers have had on our world as they strip the environment of resources, always looking to gain more.)
