/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 241 0 R
/E (It was early in the morning of April 15, 1912 when RMS Titanic disappeared into the waters of the Northern Atlantic on her maiden voyage. It only took 2 hours and 40 minutes for the largest vessel of her time to sink below the waves after striking an iceberg and taking the lives of 1635 out of the 2224 people on board. A lot of the disaster can be attributed towards poor evacuation planning & lack of a sufficient number of lifeboats. Ironically, an evacuation \(muster\) drill was planned to occur on the day of the sinking. Also, the Titanic had more of the required number of lifeboats at the time of its sailing. It is because of this tragedy that all cruises now must have their muster drills done prior to leaving port and have enough lifeboats for everyone on board.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
