448 0 obj
<<
/Title (These amphibians are highly playful and love swimming up and down natural waterfalls. But their curiosity can come with a price - lava falls are also common down below, and when the axolotls' playing gets too close... I saw several unlucky individuals meet an untimely end. Although they can regenerate, it can't save them from a near instant fiery death!)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 446 0 R
/Next 450 0 R
>>
endobj
449 0 obj
<<
/Title (This final photo came as I was packing up to exit the jungle - I turned around and there, at the horizon, was a woodland mansion.  Snagging the image of the panda cub and its parent seemingly looking out over at it is a poignant reminder of the effect the Illagers have had on our world as they strip the environment of resources, always looking to gain more.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 451 0 R
/Next 447 0 R
>>
endobj
450 0 obj
<<
/Title (Exiting the beautiful but dangerous depths, I made my way to the distant jungle, pursuing the elusive panda.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 448 0 R
/Next 451 0 R
>>
endobj
451 0 obj
<<
/Title (After many days and nights, I came across a small family group, living at the edge of a bamboo grove.  The small cub was barely the height of the wild grass, and as rambunctious as any newborn animal living without fear could be, only returning to its parents' side at nightfall.  Away from the lights of any civilization, the darkness of night was nearly complete, making low-light photos especially haunting.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 450 0 R
/Next 449 0 R
>>
endobj
